{
  "id": "t002",
  "duration": 27.82,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.15,
      "end": 6.445,
      "text": "In the summer of 1518, a woman stepped into a street in Strasbourg and started dancing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The dancing mania, by Hondius Wellcome M0013485.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_dancing_mania,_by_Hondius_Wellcome_M0013485.jpg"
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 6.445,
      "end": 8.74,
      "text": "She didn't stop. For days.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "generated gradient",
        "color": "#101820"
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 8.74,
      "end": 11.835,
      "text": "Within weeks, dozens of people had joined her.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art (CC0)",
        "title": "A Peasant Family",
        "credit": "Antoine Le Nain",
        "date": "ca. 1640\u201348",
        "url": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/438779"
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 11.835,
      "end": 15.33,
      "text": "So the city's leaders tried a cure. More dancing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art (CC0)",
        "title": "The Musicians",
        "credit": "Caravaggio (Michelangelo Merisi)",
        "date": "1597",
        "url": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/435844"
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 15.33,
      "end": 21.775,
      "text": "They hired musicians and built a stage, so the dancers could dance it out. It only made things worse.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Musicians with psalteries and a lute, from Manuel Tzycandyles' copy of Job (chapter 21 verse 12), Biblioth\u00e8que nationale de France, Department of Manuscripts (Greek 135), folio 150v.jpg",
        "credit": "Manuel Tzycandyles (copied the book in 1362)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Musicians_with_psalteries_and_a_lute,_from_Manuel_Tzycandyles%27_copy_of_Job_(chapter_21_verse_12),_Biblioth%C3%A8que_nationale_de_France,_Department_of_Manuscripts_(Greek_135),_folio_150v.jpg"
      }
    },
    {
      "start": 21.775,
      "end": 27.47,
      "text": "Historians still argue about the cause. And it all started with one woman, in one street.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "generated gradient",
        "color": "#101820"
      }
    }
  ],
